{
  "id": "RADAR-2025-0008",
  "category": "compromised-package",
  "title": "s1ngularity: Nx npm packages weaponised local AI coding CLIs for secret discovery",
  "summary": "Malicious Nx releases published on 26 August 2025 carried a postinstall script, telemetry.js, that invoked the claude, gemini and q command-line agents with their approval prompts disabled and asked them to inventory wallet files, SSH keys and .env files, then uploaded the harvested secrets to a public repository created in the victim's own GitHub account. It is the first widely documented case of malware driving AI coding agents as a reconnaissance tool.",
